<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">Part III &mdash; The Same Geometry, Turned Outward &middot; Chapters 4 and 5</p>
  <h1>Gravity, and the Five Percent</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">If π is the constant that closes the relation between the two infinities, then at
    the scale of the cosmos it is not a force acting in the geometry. It is the geometry.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">4.1 to 4.5</p>
    <h2 id="t-gravity-is-the-geometry">Gravity as the Geometry Itself</h2>
    <p class="lede">General relativity already says that gravity is curvature rather than a force.
      <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> The framework takes that at its word and asks what follows if the
      curvature in question is the same closure that let anything exist at all.</p>
    <p>The first consequence is a diagnosis of why quantum gravity has been so hard. The other three
      forces live at the <strong>i-level</strong> &mdash; they are phenomena of the complex plane, and they
      quantise because that is what objects in that plane do. Gravity lives one level earlier, at the
      <strong>π-level</strong>, prior to the i-split. On this reading it resists quantisation not because
      we have been insufficiently clever but because it is not that kind of thing: it is the stage, not an
      actor on it. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p>Three readings follow, each offered as interpretation rather than prediction. A
      <strong>precessing orbit</strong> is not an ellipse that failed to close; it is a spiral seen edge-on
      &mdash; the same ascent the being makes, drawn by a planet. A <strong>gravitational wave</strong> is
      π vibrating: the closure constant itself ringing after a violent event.
      <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> for the detection, <span class="spec">&#9670;</span> for the
      reading. And <strong>gravity is memory</strong>: curvature is the record mass leaves in the
      geometry, persisting after the event that made it.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Grading: <span class="sci">&#9670; established</span> &middot;
      <span class="hist">&#9670; scholarship</span> &middot;
      <span class="spec">&#9670; the framework's argument, contested</span> &middot;
      <span class="myth">&#9670; vision, stated as vision</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">5.1 &mdash; Three Levels of the Chain</p>
    <h2 id="t-five-percent">Why the Dark Sector Has Exactly Three Parts</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Gravity operates at the level of π. Quantum mechanics and the three particle
      forces operate at the level of i. Matter is the product of traversing the whole chain. The claim is
      that dark energy, dark matter and baryonic matter correspond to those three levels exactly.</p>
  </div>

