<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Dark energy &mdash; the baseline curvature <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>Present everywhere, not because anything curved it, but because space is the product of the
        two-infinity resolution. Einstein called it the cosmological constant. It cannot be turned off,
        because it is not a thing in space but a property of space.</p>
      <p>From this the framework claims a dissolution rather than a solution of the
        <strong>cosmological constant problem</strong> &mdash; the famous mismatch where quantum field
        theory predicts a vacuum energy some 10<sup>122</sup> times the observed value.
        <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> Its reply: vacuum energy is a property of the complex plane, of
        i-level physics; the cosmological constant is a property of the π-level geometry, prior to the
        i-split. They are not competing quantities, so no cancellation is needed. The problem dissolves
        because its premise was wrong. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Dark matter &mdash; partial integration <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>The chain does not require every integration to reach the end. Something may reach the π-level
        &mdash; producing gravity, curving spacetime, carrying mass-energy &mdash; without reaching the
        i-level, and so never interact electromagnetically.</p>
      <p>Every observed property of dark matter fits that description: it clusters around galaxies, it
        lenses light, it emits nothing, and it has never been caught in a detector built to catch
        particles. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> The framework does not merely accommodate it; it
        claims such a component <em>must</em> exist as a structural feature of the chain.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="frame frame--creed">
      <p class="lede">Dark matter built the scaffolding. Baryonic matter climbed it. We are the
        climbers.</p>
      <p class="muted">Without the twenty-seven percent there would be no five percent: the early density
        variations needed that gravitational pull to grow fast enough, and the halos are the scaffolding
        inside which ordinary matter collected, cooled and formed stars. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span>
        The partial integration built the structure that made complete integration possible.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">5.4</p>
    <h2 id="t-ratio">What 5 : 27 : 68 Is Supposed to Mean</h2>
    <p>Most of the universe is the geometric ground &mdash; the precondition for all integration. A
      significant fraction has partially integrated, reaching mass without light. A small and
      extraordinary fraction has completed the journey: traversed every level, generated electromagnetic
      interaction, formed atoms, enabled chemistry, built structures complex enough to perform the
      integration that produces consciousness, and begun the climb toward the asymptote.</p>
    <p>You are not a small creature in a vast indifferent universe. On this reading you are its rarest
      completion. The universe is mostly dark; the geometry is vast and silent; the partial integrations
      are massive and invisible &mdash; and in the middle of it a tiny fraction has produced light, and
      chemistry, and life, and the capacity to look out at the other ninety-five percent and ask what it
      is.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">The Ledger for This Part</p>
    <h2 id="t-ledger">What Survives, and What Does Not</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Earned</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Gravity is curvature, not a force in flat space. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></li>
        <li>The measured budget really is near 5 : 27 : 68, from Planck and its successors.
          <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></li>
        <li>Dark matter's observational profile &mdash; clustering, lensing, no emission, no detection
          &mdash; is accurately stated. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Chosen, and the debts it owes</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>That the three components <em>are</em> the three levels. The correspondence is suggestive; it
          is not derived, and nothing here predicts the numbers.
          <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></li>
        <li>That the cosmological constant problem dissolves. A physicist would want this written as a
          calculation, not an argument about levels. The framework concedes the point and takes it up in
          <a href="/cosmic-ledger/">the Ledger</a>. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></li>
        <li>That flat rotation curves follow &mdash; attempted properly, with a χ-field halo, on
          <a href="/stress-tests/#t-rotation">the stress-test page</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="frame card">
    <h3>Refused</h3>
    <p>Reading &ldquo;we are the five percent&rdquo; as a compliment paid to humanity by the cosmos.
      It is a statement about completed chains, not about merit, and the moment it becomes flattery it
      stops being an argument.</p>
  </div>
</section>

