<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">&mdash; the dark sector, said in one breath</p>
    <h2 id="t-dark-sector">The Dark Sector Is a Statement About Completion</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">The three parts of the budget are not three substances. On this framework's
      reading they are one process caught at three stages, and the only thing that distinguishes them is
      how far along the chain α &rarr; π &rarr; π/2 &rarr; i a region managed to get.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="frame illuminated">
      <p>Dark energy is geometry that never left the baseline: it expands, and it neither clumps nor shines.
        Dark matter is geometry that reached the π/2 threshold and halted: it has the curvature, so it
        gravitates, but the complex phase never completed, so it cannot couple to light. Baryonic matter is
        geometry that finished: curvature <em>and</em> phase, which is to say gravity and electromagnetism
        and therefore chemistry, bodies and observers. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
      <p class="lede">Dark matter is dark for a structural reason, not an accidental one. It is not a
        particle that happens to interact weakly. It is a region that stopped one link short of being able
        to interact at all.</p>
      <p>The payoff is a flat rotation curve for free. A galaxy sits in a χ-gradient falling from χ &asymp; 1
        in the disk to χ &asymp; &frac12; through the halo; a χ &prop; 1/r profile gives
        ρ &prop; 1/r², hence M(r) &prop; r, hence a constant orbital velocity out to large radii &mdash;
        which is what Vera Rubin measured and what the visible mass cannot explain. The arithmetic and the
        derivation gap are both set out in full at
        <a href="/cosmic-ledger/#t-flat-curves">the cosmic ledger</a>. The gap, in one line: the 1/r profile
        is motivated but has not been forced out of the framework's own field equations.</p>
      <p class="muted">And the limit of the claim, stated here so that it is not mistaken later: this
        account says nothing whatever about <em>which way</em> a galaxy turns. Completion and orientation
        are different axes. Spin belongs to <a href="/moebius/#t-handedness">the seam</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
