  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">Closing Stance</p>
    <p>This is the part of the framework with the most to lose from data. A single laboratory detection of
      a dark-matter particle would not refute it outright, but it would make the &ldquo;partial
      integration&rdquo; reading far less attractive than a straightforward new particle. That is a real
      falsification condition, and it is left standing rather than hedged.</p>
